{# Delivery overlay for the packaged splunk-homelab-alerts app.

   The app ships its own default/savedsearches.conf whose [default] stanza
   turns action.zammad on for every detector, but no Zammad alert action is
   configured on this instance -- Zammad and Slack are reached only through
   the ntfy hub webhook (see the header of savedsearches.conf.j2 and
   assert_alerting_gates.yml), so as shipped those detectors deliver
   nowhere. A same-app local/ file layers above the packaged default and
   item-merges with it: the dead Zammad action goes off, the hub webhook
   goes on, and every other packaged default (scheduling, tracking,
   severities) is left untouched.

   A stanza whose own body sets action.zammad = 0 is one of the app's
   scheduled reports, not a detector, and would inherit action.webhook = 1
   from the [default] above -- posting to the hub on every scheduled run.
   Each one is therefore re-disabled per stanza, derived from the INSTALLED
   file at converge time: a hand-maintained copy here would drift from the
   packaged app on its next release.

   Rendered AFTER tasks/apps.yml: that task deletes the whole app directory
   on every version upgrade, so an overlay written earlier is wiped in the
   same run.
#}
{% set report_stanzas = [] %}
{% for stanza_name, stanza_body in splunk_docker_homelab_alerts_app_conf | regex_findall('(?ms)^\[([^\]\n]+)\][ \t]*$(.*?)(?=^\[|\Z)') %}
{% if stanza_body | regex_search('(?m)^[ \t]*action\.zammad[ \t]*=[ \t]*0[ \t]*$') %}
{% set _ = report_stanzas.append(stanza_name) %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[default]
action.zammad = 0
{% if splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_url %}
action.webhook = 1
action.webhook.param.url = {{ splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_url }}{{ splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_query }}
{% endif %}
{% for stanza_name in report_stanzas %}

[{{ stanza_name }}]
action.webhook = 0
{% endfor %}
